{"step_index":184,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:10:15Z","input_tokens":2782,"cache_read_tokens":269659,"output_tokens":2864,"thinking":"The adjustment introduces a new constraint: only consume the exact quantity specified on the progress tracker. Excess cards must remain. Considering the two actions, this means we must alter the card movement logic. First, when moving cards onto a target column, we'll need to check the progress.\n\n\nWhen moving cards to a target column, calculate the number of cards needed, `need = T - m`, where `T` is the target amount and `m` is the current count.  If the source column has more cards than needed, specifically `k > need`, two interpretations are possible. The first is to move only `need` cards, leaving excess in the source.  The second is to move all `k` cards to the target column.\n\n\nThe previous logic cleared excess cards in the target column after a move. The core of the problem lies in incorrect deletion: previously, the code consumed all `count` cards if the number of cards in the destination column met or exceeded the target, thus removing excess cards. This conflicts with the new requirement to leave excess cards. This highlights that the splice operation in the existing code needs to be modified to only delete the `target` amount. Now, the `col.splice(col.length - target, target)` correctly consumes the right number.\n\n\nConsidering the two cases: transferring only the needed cards versus transferring all cards and clearing the target amount, the second case reveals important card state transitions. If only the required amount is moved (Case 1), excess cards remain in the source column, preventing further actions. Moving all cards (Case 2) results in the source column revealing a new card and the excess cards being removed. The core issue is the new requirement to leave excess cards while still removing cards from the target column that exceeds the target amount.\n\n\nThe core logic revolves around maintaining the card counts after a move or clear operation, especially when dealing with excess cards. The key insight is that, regardless of the source, only the `target` amount of cards should be consumed on the destination column, leaving excess cards. This principle applies consistently whether the cards are transferred between columns or moved from a holding slot. The focus now is on testing the edge cases of moving from the holding slot and how the excess will be handled in both the source (holding slot) and destination columns.\n\n\nThe `splice` operation, correctly applied, ensures that only the target amount is removed, preserving any excess. If the column starts with less than the target, cards will be added. When adding, any remaining cards from the source should be discarded. The key point is that we must always move all possible cards from the source. The critical behavior change is to keep the excess cards on the target after adding cards from the source, leaving the source column free for new discovery.\n\n\nThe player's action of clicking a column now triggers a card reveal, potentially changing strategic options based on which column is selected. The key is now that cards don't necessarily clear out, leaving excess cards in the receiving column which triggers the card reveal instead of the clear. This creates a decision point for the player based on which column reveals a hidden card.\n\n\nThe core mechanic centers on card reveal after a column is cleared or a move results in excess cards. Analyzing scenarios: If a column has excess cards, revealing a new card depends on whether the player clicks that column to trigger the reveal. The action determines which column reveals a new card and which retains excess cards.\n\nExamining the Holding Slot scenario: If the Holding Slot provides more cards than needed, all cards move, the destination column clears to the target amount, and any excess remains. The Slot becomes empty.\n\nConsidering cases where the count exceeds twice the target, a loop can be used to clear and retain excess until the target amount is reached.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Updated card_sort_cach_1_full_stack_outline.html so that clearing a batch only consumes the exact target number of cards shown on the progress badge and leaves any excess cards on the column.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Admin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\0ca39d47-bf1d-4d04-97dc-9c2fe64cb8c8\\\\card_sort_cach_1_full_stack_outline.html\"","Replacement":"\"            // Display Counter & Progress Bar ONLY on the very last (bottom-most) card!\\n            if (isLastCard) {\\n              const displayCount = Math.min(bottomGroupCount, target);\\n              const extraCount = bottomGroupCount - target;\\n              gCard.innerHTML = `\\n                <div class=\\\"counter-badge\\\">${ extraCount > 0 ? `${target}/${target} (+${extraCount})` : `${displayCount}/${target}` }</div>\\n                <div class=\\\"progress-track\\\">\\n                  <div class=\\\"progress-fill\\\" style=\\\"width: ${pct}%\\\"></div>\\n                </div>\\n              `;\\n            }\\n\\n            groupBox.appendChild(gCard);\"","Target":"\"            // Display Counter & Progress Bar ONLY on the very last (bottom-most) card!\\n            if (isLastCard) {\\n              gCard.innerHTML = `\\n                <div class=\\\"counter-badge\\\">${bottomGroupCount}/${target}</div>\\n                <div class=\\\"progress-track\\\">\\n                  <div class=\\\"progress-fill\\\" style=\\\"width: ${pct}%\\\"></div>\\n                </div>\\n              `;\\n            }\\n\\n            groupBox.appendChild(gCard);\""}}]}
{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:11:04Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-16T16:11:04+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-16T16:11:06+07:00\nMade 1 replacement in C:\\Users\\Admin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\0ca39d47-bf1d-4d04-97dc-9c2fe64cb8c8\\card_sort_cach_1_full_stack_outline.html starting at line 475 (+3/-1 lines)."}
{"step_index":186,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T09:11:06Z","input_tokens":3019,"cache_read_tokens":272442,"output_tokens":1071,"thinking":"The `checkAndClearBatch` function requires modification to selectively remove cards. The current implementation removes all cards. The goal is to remove only the `target` number of cards from each column. After the change, `count - target` cards will remain in the column.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Update checkAndClearBatch to only remove exactly `target` cards and preserve leftover cards on the column.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Admin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\0ca39d47-bf1d-4d04-97dc-9c2fe64cb8c8\\\\card_sort_cach_1_full_stack_outline.html\"","Replacement":"\"    async function checkAndClearBatch(colIdx) {\\n      const col = columns[colIdx];\\n      if (col.length === 0) return;\\n\\n      while (col.length > 0) {\\n        const count = getBottomGroupCount(col);\\n        const color = col[col.length - 1];\\n        const target = getTargetForColor(color);\\n\\n        if (count < target) break;\\n\\n        const leftover = count - target;\\n        render();\\n\\n        // Animate only the `target` cards being consumed (or whole group if leftover === 0)\\n        const groupEl = document.getElementById(`group-col-${colIdx}`);\\n        if (groupEl) {\\n          if (leftover === 0) {\\n            groupEl.classList.add('clearing-anim');\\n          } else {\\n            const cardEls = groupEl.querySelectorAll('.group-card');\\n            for (let i = leftover; i < cardEls.length; i++) {\\n              cardEls[i].classList.add('clearing-anim');\\n            }\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        if (leftover > 0) {\\n          setStatus(`💥 Cột ${colIdx + 1} nổ đúng ${target}/${target} lá ${COLORS[color].name} ➔ Để lại ${leftover} lá thừa!`);\\n        } else {\\n          setStatus(`💥 Cột ${colIdx + 1} gom đủ ${target}/${target} lá ${COLORS[color].name} ➔ NỔ CLEAR!`);\\n        }\\n\\n        await sleep(240);\\n        // Remove ONLY `target` cards, leaving `leftover` cards on the column!\\n        col.splice(col.length - target, target);\\n        render();\\n      }\\n\\n      const totalLeft = columns.reduce((acc, c) => acc + c.length, 0) + (holdingSlot ? holdingSlot.count : 0);\\n      if (totalLeft === 0) {\\n        setStatus('🎉 CHIẾN THẮNG! Bạn đã phá đảo toàn bộ bức tranh Pixel!');\\n      }\\n    }\"","Target":"\"    async function checkAndClearBatch(colIdx) {\\n      const col = columns[colIdx];\\n      if (col.length === 0) return;\\n\\n      const count = getBottomGroupCount(col);\\n      const color = col[col.length - 1];\\n      const target = getTargetForColor(color);\\n\\n      if (count >= target) {\\n        render();\\n        const groupEl = document.getElementById(`group-col-${colIdx}`);\\n        if (groupEl) groupEl.classList.add('clearing-anim');\\n        setStatus(`💥 Cột ${colIdx + 1} gom đủ cụm ${count}/${target} lá ${COLORS[color].name} ➔ NỔ CLEAR CẢ CỤM!`);\\n        await sleep(240);\\n        col.splice(col.length - count, count);\\n        render();\\n\\n        const totalLeft = columns.reduce((acc, c) => acc + c.length, 0) + (holdingSlot ? holdingSlot.count : 0);\\n        if (totalLeft === 0) {\\n          setStatus('🎉 CHIẾN THẮNG! Bạn đã phá đảo toàn bộ bức tranh Pixel!');\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\""}}]}
